WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.676
Users have a user name, an email address, and roles.

00:00:04.676 --> 00:00:09.304
Custom user settings add fields of your own, such as a nickname, as

00:00:09.304 --> 00:00:11.395
tabs on the Edit User page.

00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:17.100
In this video, we create a section, fill it in, grant access, and export its values.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.367
A site often needs more information about a user than the built-in details,

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.133
such as a nickname or a newsletter choice.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:33.800
Custom user settings define those fields in the admin, using content types.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.931
Each group of fields is a section.

00:00:36.931 --> 00:00:41.811
A section is a content type marked with the stereotype Custom User Settings.

00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:46.930
Every section becomes a tab on the Edit User page, named after the content type.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.716
The tasks are to enable the feature, create a section, fill it in

00:00:51.716 --> 00:00:55.468
for a user, and share it, by granting a permission to a role

00:00:55.468 --> 00:00:57.230
and exporting the values.

00:01:01.425 --> 00:01:05.085
Custom User Settings is a feature of the Users module.

00:01:05.085 --> 00:01:08.989
Open Tools, Features, and search for Custom User Settings.

00:01:08.989 --> 00:01:11.795
Users and Contents are its dependencies.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.366
Select Enable.

00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:17.550
A message confirms that the feature Custom User Settings was enabled.

00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:23.820
A section is a content type.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.584
Create a dedicated type for each section, because the documentation warns against marking

00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:32.253
a type that already has content items.

00:01:32.253 --> 00:01:37.167
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and select Create new type.

00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:40.246
Enter User Profile as the Display Name.

00:01:40.246 --> 00:01:42.695
The Technical Name fills in from it.

00:01:42.695 --> 00:01:43.861
Select Create.

00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:47.558
The next page offers parts to add to the type.

00:01:47.558 --> 00:01:50.986
This section only needs fields, so select Cancel.

00:01:51.457 --> 00:01:53.318
Fields hold the values.

00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:58.516
Select Add Field, enter Nickname as the Display Name, choose the Field Type

00:01:58.516 --> 00:02:00.697
Text Field, and select Save.

00:02:01.151 --> 00:02:03.418
Add a second field the same way.

00:02:03.418 --> 00:02:07.356
Name it Newsletter, and choose the Field Type Boolean Field.

00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:09.861
Both fields are listed under Fields.

00:02:10.324 --> 00:02:15.344
A section is not content that editors create, list, or publish.

00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:21.964
So clear Creatable, Listable, Draftable, Versionable, and Securable, and select Save.

00:02:22.427 --> 00:02:25.011
Select Edit on User Profile again.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:31.408
Once the stereotype is saved, the editor hides Creatable, Listable, Draftable and Versionable

00:02:31.408 --> 00:02:35.543
and leaves their values alone, so they were cleared first.

00:02:35.543 --> 00:02:40.647
Enter Custom User Settings without spaces in Stereotype, and select Save.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:45.003
The list shows the stereotype as a badge on User Profile.

00:02:45.003 --> 00:02:49.279
The type is a section, and it adds a tab to the Edit User page.

00:02:53.578 --> 00:02:57.909
Open Access Control, Users, and select Edit for the user jamie.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:02.868
Beside the tab with the account fields, a tab named User Profile appears.

00:03:03.335 --> 00:03:05.266
Select the User Profile tab.

00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:07.595
It shows the fields of the section:

00:03:07.595 --> 00:03:10.605
a Nickname text box and a Newsletter check box.

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:15.196
Enter Jamie as the nickname, check Newsletter, and select Save.

00:03:15.196 --> 00:03:18.247
A message confirms that the user was updated.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.906
Select Edit for the same user again.

00:03:20.906 --> 00:03:24.550
The tab shows the saved nickname and the checked Newsletter box.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.876
Add User opens the Create User page, which shows the same tab, so

00:03:28.876 --> 00:03:32.204
a section can be filled in while an account is created.

00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:39.146
Each section has its own permission.

00:03:39.146 --> 00:03:44.128
Open Access Control, Roles, and select Edit for a role, such as Editor.

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:47.247
In Search permissions, enter Custom User.

00:03:47.247 --> 00:03:52.078
The permission is named Manage Own Custom User Settings, followed by the display

00:03:52.078 --> 00:03:54.157
name of the type, User Profile.

00:03:54.628 --> 00:03:56.689
Check Allow, and select Save.

00:03:56.689 --> 00:04:00.989
People in this role see the User Profile tab when they edit a user.

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:03.698
Editing a user is a separate permission.

00:04:04.169 --> 00:04:07.332
The Administrator role has every permission.

00:04:07.332 --> 00:04:13.529
A role with Manage security settings and all users also has the permission of every section.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:22.469
To move the values to another site, add a step to a deployment plan.

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:28.049
Open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and select Manage Steps for the plan Team profiles.

00:04:28.502 --> 00:04:32.449
Select Add Step, and find the Custom User Settings card.

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:37.159
It says that the step exports all or specified custom user settings.

00:04:37.159 --> 00:04:38.242
Choose Add.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.222
The step includes all custom user settings by default.

00:04:42.222 --> 00:04:47.139
Clearing Include all custom user settings lets you choose sections one by one.

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:48.310
Select Create.

00:04:48.765 --> 00:04:51.388
The plan lists the step with the badge All.

00:04:51.388 --> 00:04:55.081
On the other site, an import fills in the sections of the users

00:04:55.081 --> 00:04:58.025
that have the same user ID, and skips the others.

00:05:00.025 --> 00:05:04.755
Custom user settings turn content types into tabs on the Edit User page,

00:05:04.755 --> 00:05:08.818
and the documentation page covers the details for developers.

00:05:08.818 --> 00:05:10.395
Thanks for watching.

